Your deliverable: a one-page SLO proposal for a sample checkout API, written as if you will defend it in a design review.
- **Choose three SLIs** from the four golden signals (e.g. request success rate, p99 latency under 300 ms, saturation of the checkout workers), and justify each choice in one sentence.
- **Set SLO targets and a 30-day window** for each, then compute the error budget in minutes the way the Worked estimation shows.
- **Write the release policy** as a rule: budget remaining → ship; budget exhausted → freeze. Name who decides.
- **Specify two burn-rate alerts**: one fast-burn (pages) and one slow-burn (tickets), with the metric each watches.
- **Defend it aloud in 10 minutes**, then write the three hardest questions you were asked and your improved answers.
Reference shelf (module sources): **Google SRE Books** (https://sre.google/) — SLIs/SLOs, incidents, and reliability math from the source. **Prometheus Documentation** (https://prometheus.io/docs/) — metrics, PromQL, and alerting references.

