Your deliverable: a full mock incident on a sample scenario — the checkout API is returning 500s for 20% of requests — run end to end, then written up.
- **Run the drill** using the Hands-on procedure: declare, assign roles, mitigate (choose rollback vs shed-load and defend the choice aloud), hold comms cadence.
- **Produce the timeline** as the scribe would: timestamps, decisions, who made them.
- **Write the blameless postmortem**: impact statement, five-whys down to a systemic cause, and three action items each with an owner and a date.
- **Add the severity call**: what severity you declared, why, and who got paged under your paging policy.
- **Debrief**: what broke down in your process (not the fake system), and the one change you'll make before the next drill.
Reference shelf (module sources): **Google SRE Books** (https://sre.google/) — incident response chapters from the source. **CISA Resources & Tools** (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools) — US government guidance on incident response and best practice.

