Your deliverable: an alerting-policy document plus dashboard sketch for a sample three-tier service.
- **Dashboard sketch**: golden signals up top, drill-down paths, deploy annotations, time-range comparisons — organized by the questions on-call asks at 3am.
- **Alerting policy table**: each alert named, its signal, its threshold or burn rate, and its route (page vs ticket) with a one-sentence justification.
- **Tracing plan**: which service boundaries get instrumented first and what question the traces answer (latency attribution across services).
- **Cardinality budget**: the label set with a written rule for what may never become a label.
- **Present it as a 10-minute design review**, then record the two objections raised and your revised answers.
