- **Mock circuit** — the full simulated loop: incident round, metrics/SLO round, system-design round, behavioral round, run back-to-back under time.
- **Round shape** — the fixed structure each round type follows: rehearse the shape and the method becomes automatic under pressure.
- **Interview rubric** — fixed scoring axes per round (correctness, complexity analysis, communication, time management, tradeoffs named): turns feelings into triage data.
- **Debrief log** — the written record after every mock: what leaked, its category, the redrill plan. Improvement lives here, not in doing more mocks.
- **Weakness-targeting week** — the week between simulation and the real loop, spent only on the lowest rubric scores: raise the floor, not the ceiling.
- **Taper** — the final two weeks: no new material, redrill weak patterns, full timed mocks, fix sleep, rehearse the story bank aloud.
- **48-hour checklist** — logistics, rest, rehearsed stories, no new topics: the last two days convert preparation into performance.

