Your deliverable: a scored mock-loop dossier.
- **The schedule**: your four-round loop day with times, roles, and the rubric each round is scored against.
- **Score sheets**: one per round, every axis scored honestly — correctness, communication, time management, tradeoffs named.
- **The debrief**: the two lowest-scoring axes, the category of each miss (not just the instance), and a one-week redrill plan with verification.
- **The 48-hour checklist**: your personal version — logistics, sleep, story bank, what you will explicitly not study.
- **Reflection**: one paragraph on which round shape still isn't automatic, and the drill that will make it so.
Reference shelf (module sources): **Google SRE Books** (https://sre.google/) — the reliability material the mocks draw on.

