Your deliverable: a pipeline design document for a sample service, written as a design-review artifact.
- **Pipeline diagram**: stages in order with durations, gates, and owners; the artifact and its tagging scheme.
- **Strategy matrix**: blue-green vs canary vs rolling per environment, with the blast-radius reasoning.
- **Rollback runbook**: triggers, commands, and the decision rule — when you roll back vs fix forward.
- **Pipeline-as-code**: the workflow file layout in the repo and how changes to it are reviewed.
- **Present it as a 10-minute design round**, then answer: 'your canary metrics look fine but users complain — what now?' in writing.
Reference shelf (module sources): **GitHub Actions Documentation** (https://docs.github.com/en/actions) — pipeline-as-code reference. **Jenkins Documentation** (https://jenkins.io/doc/) — the classic CI server most interview pipelines were built on.

