Build the platform scaffold on paper, in order, in 40 minutes.
1. **Lay out the repo.** `app/` (code + Dockerfile), `infra/` (Terraform: VPC, cluster), `pipeline/` (CI workflows), `gitops/` (Argo CD app manifests), `docs/` (ADRs, runbooks). Justify each directory.
2. **Terraform the VPC.** Module with public/private subnets, NAT, route tables — the network the cluster will live on.
3. **Script the bootstrap.** Every cluster-creation step as a script or IaC: no clicks. State why: reproducible, reviewable, auditable.
4. **Wire the CI pipeline.** Lint → test → build → scan → push SHA-tagged image — the pipeline from the CI/CD module, reused.
5. **Add the GitOps deploy.** Argo CD watches the repo; merges to main reconcile the cluster. Narrate the drift story: manual changes get reverted automatically.
6. **Write one ADR and one runbook.** ADR: why Argo CD over push-based deploys. Runbook: pods CrashLooping — the triage procedure from the troubleshooting module.

