Your deliverable: a one-page 'cloud concepts' briefing you'd give a skeptical CTO.
- **The primitives**: regions/AZs/edge, shared responsibility, and the VM/container/serverless decision tree — each with its 'when it wins'.
- **The worked estimation** from this module, with assumptions labeled as assumptions.
- **The honest value props**: what the cloud genuinely buys (elasticity, managed heavy lifting, speed) and what it doesn't (automatic savings, automatic security).
- **The trap answers**: 'the cloud is secure' (no — your bucket policy is your job), 'it's always cheaper' (no — FinOps or surprise).
- **Present it in 10 minutes**, then take the hardest pushback question and answer it in writing.
Reference shelf (module sources): **AWS Documentation** (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/) — compute, networking, data, and security primitives. **Google Cloud Documentation** (https://cloud.google.com/docs) — GCP-side primitives for vendor-neutral depth.

