Your deliverable: a network design + troubleshooting guide for a sample three-tier VPC.
- **The design**: VPC with public/private subnets across 2 AZs, route tables, NAT, security groups (stateful, least-privilege), NACLs (stateless, explicit both ways), ALB in public, app and data in private.
- **The rules table**: every security-group and NACL rule with its justification — 'each answers a how-do-these-networks-talk question.'
- **The dead-connection runbook**: the six-layer bisection from the Hands-on procedure as a checklist.
- **The DNS section**: public vs private hosted zones, TTL strategy for an upcoming migration, health-checked failover.
- **Present the design in 10 minutes**, then debug a seeded fault (wrong NACL) live.
Reference shelf (module sources): **AWS Documentation** (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/) — networking primitives. **Google Cloud Documentation** (https://cloud.google.com/docs) — GCP networking for vendor-neutral depth.

