Your deliverable: the complete architecture package — the portfolio piece.
- **Requirements and constraints** in one page: users, scale, latency, compliance, budget.
- **The reference architecture**: three-tier across 2 AZs, every component justified, every arrow labeled.
- **IaC for the whole stack**: the module layout that builds it reproducibly.
- **The cost estimate** from the Worked estimation, assumptions labeled, Cadillac and Honda both shown.
- **The failure-mode review**: per component — what breaks, how it degrades, whether that's acceptable.
- **One ADR**: the highest-stakes decision, with alternatives and consequences.
- **Walk an interviewer through it in 15 minutes**, from requirements to the cost slide.
Reference shelf (module sources): **AWS Well-Architected Framework** (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/welcome.html) — the six pillars; the architecture interview's rubric. **Terraform Documentation** (https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/docs) — IaC references.

