Your deliverable: a code-review finding writeup — the portfolio piece.
- **Pick one vulnerability class** (XSS, IDOR, SSRF, or injection) and write the full finding: the code pattern, why it's exploitable, the fix, and how you'd verify the fix.
- **Add the Top 10 framing**: which risk category it belongs to and a second example of the same category.
- **Include the review checklist** you used — the trust-boundary-first procedure from this module.
- **Sanitize everything**: no real company code, no real hostnames — method transfers, specifics don't need to.
- **Present it in 10 minutes** as 'here's how I found one in code review and what the fix was.'
Reference shelf (module sources): **OWASP** (https://owasp.org/) — the Top 10 and project pages. **OWASP Cheat Sheet Series** (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/) — concise defensive guidance on auth, crypto, and injection.

