Your deliverable: a network security design review for a sample three-tier system.
- **The zone diagram** with explicit allow-rules per boundary — east-west included.
- **The TLS section**: handshake walkthrough, version/cipher policy, cert lifecycle (ACME + expiry monitoring), HSTS, and where pinning applies.
- **The zero-trust overlay**: identity, device posture, and continuous verification per access path.
- **DNS and DDoS sections**: the hardening checklist and the layered mitigation plan.
- **Findings, consultant-style**: risk-ranked, business impact, concrete fixes with effort estimates.
- **Present in 10 minutes**, ending with: 'the VPN perimeter is dead; every request authenticates and authorizes.'
Reference shelf (module sources): **CISA Resources & Tools** (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools) — hardening and best-practice guidance. **NIST Cybersecurity Framework** (https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework) — the Identify/Protect/Detect/Respond/Recover frame.

