Your deliverable: a crypto review one-pager for a sample service.
- **The password-storage design**: algorithm, salt, work factor, pepper — with the 'why not SHA-256' reasoning.
- **The TLS posture**: versions, ciphers, cert lifecycle, HSTS — handshake plus hygiene.
- **The key-management design**: where keys live, rotation schedule and triggers, per-environment separation, audit.
- **The randomness audit**: every token/nonce/key source checked against the CSPRNG rule.
- **The never-build list**: what this service will never implement itself, and the vetted primitive for each.
- **Present in 10 minutes**, ending with the never-roll-your-own rule and what it costs to break it.
Reference shelf (module sources): **OWASP Cheat Sheet Series** (https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/) — crypto and password-storage guidance. **NIST Cybersecurity Framework** (https://www.nist.gov/cyberframework) — the Protect function framing.

