Your deliverable: a detection-engineering brief plus a breach-story rehearsal.
- **The detection brief**: ATT&CK technique, log source verification, rule logic, tuning rationale (precision/recall), and the adversary-simulation test.
- **Coverage map**: three techniques across three tactics, each mapped to its log source — coverage measured against the matrix, not vibes.
- **The breach story**: a sanitized incident told blameless — timeline as understood then, what investigation showed, action items with owners, what you personally changed.
- **The IR phase card**: the six NIST phases on one page, with the contain-before-eradicate rule highlighted.
- **Present the detection in 10 minutes**, then tell the breach story in 5 — and take the follow-up questions.
Reference shelf (module sources): **MITRE ATT&CK** (https://attack.mitre.org/) — the tactic/technique matrix. **CISA Resources & Tools** (https://www.cisa.gov/resources-tools) — incident-response guidance.

