Run a 45-minute DSA speed-rep session — the sport's training unit.
1. **Pick the pattern batch.** Today: trees/graphs/heaps (traversals, BFS/DFS, top-k). Tomorrow: DP basics (1D ladder, knapsack shapes). One batch per session.
2. **Set the timer: 30 minutes per problem.** Budget aloud before starting: 5 clarify + plan, 20 code, 5 test.
3. **Clarify first.** Restate the problem, name the edge cases, state the pattern you suspect and why.
4. **Brute force, stated.** Write it, state its complexity — the honest baseline — then optimize the bottleneck.
5. **Narrate complexity at every step.** 'This loop is O(n) because…' — said out loud, every rep. Silent reps train half the interview.
6. **Debrief by category.** For each miss: wrong pattern, bug, complexity fumble, or time — then redrill the category, not the problem.

