Your deliverable: a personal DSA playbook — the pattern reference you'd trust in a loop.
- **One page per pattern**: two pointers, sliding window, BFS/DFS, heaps, DP basics — the recognition triggers, the template shape, the complexity.
- **The complexity cheat**: Big-O for the common operations, written from understanding — the analysis you state aloud.
- **Your miss log**: every recent miss classified by category, with the redrill that fixed it.
- **The 30-minute bar card**: the time budget, the brute-force rule, the test checklist — on one index card.
- **Two timed sets per week**, debriefed by category, until the narration is reflex.
Reference shelf (module sources): **NeetCode** (https://neetcode.io/) — pattern-organized DSA practice for the speed reps. **Big-O Cheat Sheet** (https://www.bigocheatsheet.com/) — complexity quick-reference for the analysis-aloud drills.

