Your deliverable: three classic design one-pagers — shortener, feed, chat.
- **Each one-pager**: requirements (functional + non-functional), the worked estimation, the 2–3 key decisions, the scaling story, the bottleneck walk.
- **The labeled diagram**: every arrow labeled with what flows — 'the labels are where the design lives.'
- **The lesson line** per classic: what this design teaches that transfers to the next question.
- **The follow-up bank**: the five hardest questions per design, answered in writing.
- **Rehearse each aloud in 30 minutes**, then have a partner attack the bottlenecks.
Reference shelf (module sources): **System Design Primer** (https://github.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer) — the classic designs and tradeoffs. **AWS Well-Architected Framework** (https://docs.aws.amazon.com/wellarchitected/latest/framework/welcome.html) — the architecture interview's rubric.

