Build the story bank in one focused weekend.
1. **List ten prompts.** Conflict, failure, leadership, ownership, disagreement, mistake, tight deadline, difficult stakeholder, mentoring, proudest work.
2. **Draft each in STAR.** Two sentences of situation, your task, the bulk on YOUR actions and decisions, a measurable result plus the lesson.
3. **Time each to 2 minutes.** Behavioral answers ramble past 3; the timer is the editor.
4. **Record all ten aloud.** Listen back like an interviewer: cut filler, cut throat-clearing, keep the decisions.
5. **Write 'why this company' with specifics.** Their product, a technical challenge, something from an employee or post, your mapping to it — interchangeable answers fail.
6. **Prepare your questions.** The four reality-revealing questions; practice hearing team health in the answers.

